1
00:05:38,181 --> 00:05:44,181
Love is the only inspiration.

2
00:11:16,363 --> 00:11:22,363
Shakespeare in Love is a romance, history, comedy film directed by John Madden.

3
00:16:54,545 --> 00:17:00,545
Young William Shakespeare is forced to stage his latest comedy, 'Romeo and
Ethel, the Pirate's Daughter', before it's even written.

4
00:22:32,727 --> 00:22:38,727
When lovely noblewoman Viola de Lesseps auditions for a role, they fall into
forbidden love — and Shakespeare's play finds a new life (and title).

5
00:28:10,909 --> 00:28:16,909
As their relationship intensifies, the comedy soon transforms into tragedy.

6
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:55,090
Will Shakespeare, played by Joseph Fiennes.

7
00:39:27,272 --> 00:39:33,272
Viola De Lesseps, played by Gwyneth Paltrow.

8
00:45:05,454 --> 00:45:11,454
Philip Henslowe, played by Geoffrey Rush.

9
00:50:43,636 --> 00:50:49,636
Hugh Fennyman, played by Tom Wilkinson.

10
00:56:21,818 --> 00:56:27,818
Queen Elizabeth, played by Judi Dench.

11
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Nurse, played by Imelda Staunton.

12
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
Shakespeare in Love is a 1998 romantic comedy period film directed by
John Madden, and written by Marc Norman and Tom Stoppard.

13
01:13:16,363 --> 01:13:22,363
It stars Gwyneth Paltrow, Joseph Fiennes, Geoffrey Rush,
Colin Firth, Ben Affleck, and Judi Dench.

14
01:18:54,545 --> 01:19:00,545
The film depicts a fictional love affair involving playwright William Shakespeare
(Fiennes) and Viola de Lesseps (Paltrow) during the writing of Romeo and Juliet.

15
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
Several characters are based on historical figures, and many of the
characters, lines, and plot devices allude to Shakespeare's plays.

16
01:30:10,909 --> 01:30:16,909
Shakespeare in Love was released on 11 December 1998 in the United States by Miramax
Films, and 29 January 1999 in the United Kingdom, by Universal Pictures.

17
01:35:49,090 --> 01:35:55,090
The film received acclaim from critics, grossed $289 million against a $25
million budget, and was the ninth-highest-grossing film of 1998.

18
01:41:27,272 --> 01:41:33,272
It received numerous accolades, including winning three Golden Globe Awards (including Best Picture and Best Actress for Paltrow), two Screen
Actors Guild Awards (Outstanding Cast and Best Actress for Paltrow), and four British Academy Film Awards (including Best Film).

19
01:47:05,454 --> 01:47:11,454
It won a leading seven Oscars out of thirteen nominations at the 71st Academy Awards: Best Picture, Best Actress for Paltrow,
Best Supporting Actress for Dench, Best Screenplay, Best Score, Best Art Direction, and Best Costume Design.

20
01:52:43,636 --> 01:52:49,636
The film explores themes of london, england, theater play,
queen elizabeth i, playwright, cross dressing.

21
01:58:21,818 --> 01:58:27,818
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
